<section data-mw-section-id="5" id="mw5A"><h4 data-mw-wikitext="" id="Sirenian_research">Sirenian research</h4>
<ul id="mw5Q"><li id="mw5g">A study on the phylogenetic relationships and evolutionary history of extant and fossil sirenians is published by Heritage &amp; Seiffert (2022).<sup about="#mwt63" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-16" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-16"}}'><a href="./2022_in_paleomammalogy#cite_note-16" id="mw5w"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mw6A"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mw6Q">[</span>16<span class="cite-bracket" id="mw6g">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mw6w">Description of the anatomy of the skull of <i id="mw7A"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Sobrarbesiren" title="Sobrarbesiren" id="mw7Q">Sobrarbesiren</a> cardieli</i> and a study on the affinities of this taxon is published by Díaz-Berenguer <i id="mw7g">et al.</i> (2022).<sup about="#mwt66" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-17" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-17"}}'><a href="./2022_in_paleomammalogy#cite_note-17" id="mw7w"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mw8A"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mw8Q">[</span>17<span class="cite-bracket" id="mw8g">]</span></span></a></sup></li></ul>

