<p id="mwC9Q">Solounias, Smith &amp; Rios Ibàñez</p></td>
<td id="mwC9U">
<p id="mwC9Y">Miocene</p></td>
<td id="mwC9c">
<p id="mwC9g">Chinji Formation</p></td>
<td id="mwC9k">
<p id="mwC9o"><span class="flagicon nowrap" about="#mwt625" typeof="mw:Transclusion" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"Flag","href":"./Template:Flag"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Pakistan"}},"i":0}}]}' id="mwC9s"><span class="mw-image-border" typeof="mw:File"><span><img resource="./File:Flag_of_Pakistan.svg" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/32/Flag_of_Pakistan.svg/40px-Flag_of_Pakistan.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/32/Flag_of_Pakistan.svg/60px-Flag_of_Pakistan.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" alt="" data-file-width="900" data-file-height="600" data-file-type="drawing" height="15" width="23" class="mw-file-element"/></span></span> </span><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Pakistan" title="Pakistan" about="#mwt625" id="mwC9w">Pakistan</a></p></td>
<td id="mwC90">
<p id="mwC94">A member of the family Giraffidae, possibly a relative of the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Okapi" title="Okapi" id="mwC98">okapi</a>. The type species is <i id="mwC-A">U. pilbeami</i>. The generic name is shared with the hymenopteran genus <i id="mwC-E">Ua</i> Girault (1929).<sup about="#mwt628" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-165" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-165"}}'><a href="./2022_in_paleomammalogy#cite_note-165" id="mwC-I"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwC-M"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC-Q">[</span>165<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC-U">]</span></span></a></sup></p></td>
