<p id="mwFiw">Eocene (<a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Itaboraian" title="Itaboraian" id="mwFi0">Itaboraian</a>)</p></td>
<td id="mwFi4">
<p id="mwFi8">Lumbrera Formation</p></td>
<td id="mwFjA">
<p id="mwFjE"><span class="flagicon nowrap" about="#mwt1209" typeof="mw:Transclusion" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"Flag","href":"./Template:Flag"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Argentina"}},"i":0}}]}' id="mwFjI"><span class="mw-image-border" typeof="mw:File"><span><img resource="./File:Flag_of_Argentina.svg" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1a/Flag_of_Argentina.svg/40px-Flag_of_Argentina.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1a/Flag_of_Argentina.svg/60px-Flag_of_Argentina.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" alt="" data-file-width="800" data-file-height="500" data-file-type="drawing" height="14" width="23" class="mw-file-element"/></span></span> </span><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Argentina" title="Argentina" about="#mwt1209" id="mwFjM">Argentina</a></p></td>
<td id="mwFjQ">
<p id="mwFjU">A <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./South_American_native_ungulates" title="South American native ungulates" id="mwFjY">South American native ungulate</a>, possibly a relative of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Mioclaenidae" title="Mioclaenidae" class="mw-redirect" id="mwFjc">mioclaenids</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Litopterna" title="Litopterna" id="mwFjg">litopterns</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Didolodontidae" title="Didolodontidae" id="mwFjk">didolodontids</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Phenacodontidae" title="Phenacodontidae" id="mwFjo">phenacodontids</a>. The type species is <i id="mwFjs">K. churcalensis</i>.</p></td>
