<section data-mw-section-id="34" id="mwGCA"><h3 data-mw-wikitext="" id="Miscellaneous_eutherian_research">Miscellaneous eutherian research</h3>
<ul id="mwGCE"><li id="mwGCI">A study on the life history of <i id="mwGCM"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Pantolambda" title="Pantolambda" id="mwGCQ">Pantolambda</a> bathmodon</i>, inferred from bone histology and geochemistry, is published by Funston <i id="mwGCU">et al.</i> (2022), who interpret their findings as indicative of an approximately 7-months-long gestation, rapid dental development and an approximately 30–to-75-days-long suckling interval, and infer that, unlike non-placental mammals and known Mesozoic precursors, <i id="mwGCY">P. bathmodon</i> was highly precocial, reproducing like a placental.<sup about="#mwt1320" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-365" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-365"}}'><a href="./2022_in_paleomammalogy#cite_note-365" id="mwGCc"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwGCg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwGCk">[</span>365<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwGCo">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwGCs">A study on the teeth eruption sequence, the sequence of cusp mineralisation and the cranial growth of <i id="mwGCw"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Alcidedorbignya" title="Alcidedorbignya" id="mwGC0">Alcidedorbignya</a> inopinata</i>, as well as on the mortality profile of the assemblage of members of this species from Tiupampa (<a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Bolivia" title="Bolivia" id="mwGC4">Bolivia</a>), is published by de Muizon &amp; Billet (2022).<sup about="#mwt1323" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-366" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-366"}}'><a href="./2022_in_paleomammalogy#cite_note-366" id="mwGC8"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwGDA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwGDE">[</span>366<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwGDI">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwGDM">A study on the age of fossil material, anatomy and phylogenetic relationships of <i id="mwGDQ"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Propyrotherium" title="Propyrotherium" id="mwGDU">Propyrotherium</a> saxeum</i>, based on data from the most complete specimen found to date, is published by Vera <i id="mwGDY">et al.</i> (2022).<sup about="#mwt1326" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-367" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-367"}}'><a href="./2022_in_paleomammalogy#cite_note-367" id="mwGDc"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwGDg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwGDk">[</span>367<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwGDo">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwGDs">A study on the affinities of extinct South American native ungulates, reassessing the study of Avilla &amp; Mothé (2021) that recovered some of these ungulates were relatives of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Hyracoidea" title="Hyracoidea" id="mwGDw">hyracoids</a>,<sup about="#mwt1329" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-368" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-368"}}'><a href="./2022_in_paleomammalogy#cite_note-368" id="mwGD0"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwGD4"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwGD8">[</span>368<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwGEA">]</span></span></a></sup> is published by Kramarz &amp; Macphee (2022), who recover all South American native ungulates as nested within <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Boreoeutheria" title="Boreoeutheria" id="mwGEE">Boreoeutheria</a>.<sup about="#mwt1332" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-369" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-369"}}'><a href="./2022_in_paleomammalogy#cite_note-369" id="mwGEI"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwGEM"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwGEQ">[</span>369<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwGEU">]</span></span></a></sup></li></ul>

